WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.033
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:06.167
I have many questions
to ask about this.

00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:09.567
Two years ago, you were --
you were in high school, right,

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:11.234
graduating high school?

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:14.634
-[ Laughs ] I graduated
in the spring of 2020, yeah.

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:17.067
-Yeah.
-So I didn't really graduate.

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:19.334
-Wow. So you didn't know,
I guess. Yeah, well.

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:22.434
-Well, I mean, it's COVID, so.
-Yes.

00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:26.400
-It was very anticlimactic.
-Yeah, for a lot of kids, yeah.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.067
-Oh, man.
But, yeah, I --

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:31.767
shortly after that,
I got into like a few --

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:33.434
I auditioned for like
a few theater schools

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:37.000
and drama programs and I got in,

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.834
but doing theater in front
of a computer for a year

00:00:40.834 --> 00:00:43.334
seemed horrible!

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:44.701
[ Laughter ]
So, I didn't go.

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:47.067
I put a year off and, instead,
did nothing for a year.

00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:49.367
-you did nothing for a year?
-Which was still horrible.

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:50.934
-Yeah.
And then you -- then --

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:55.133
then you end up a lead
in a Steven Spielberg movie.

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:56.501
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:56.501 --> 00:00:57.801
And you go --
-Yeah.

00:00:57.801 --> 00:01:01.968
-So keep -- don't stop
believing, everybody, yeah.

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:03.367
So then, now,
you're auditioning.

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:05.934
Now, you're kind of working --
I mean, auditioning.

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:06.968
You get the part.

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:08.133
Steven Spielberg's
directing you

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:10.200
and he goes, "And action,"

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.667
and you're doing him
in front of him.

00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:13.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.634 --> 00:01:14.901
-Yeah.
-I was just run

00:01:14.901 --> 00:01:15.868
out of the building.

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:17.100
[ Laughter ]
-That's -- It's --

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.200
It was nerve-wracking.
-It must be.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.601
-It was spooky, you know?

00:01:20.601 --> 00:01:22.133
-Boy, oh, boy.
-Yeah.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:23.467
-That must be pressure
right there.

00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:26.400
-Oh, yeah. But, I mean,
it's such a loving set

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.801
and everyone was so, so lovely.

00:01:28.801 --> 00:01:31.868
-Paul Dano. What a cast.
-Oh, yeah. Yeah.

00:01:31.868 --> 00:01:33.567
Michelle Williams.
I mean, just like --

00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:36.300
Did they give you advice
or they were --

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.567
-I --
-were you cool?

00:01:37.567 --> 00:01:39.400
I, um --

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.200
I asked them,
every once in a while.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.400
I remember I'd go up to Paul.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.634
I'm like, "How do you like
get into this?

00:01:45.634 --> 00:01:47.000
How do you work up to this?

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.501
Or how do you do something
like this, this emotional?"

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:51.167
And he'd be like...

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:55.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.634 --> 00:01:57.934
And then --
-That's the advice?

00:01:57.934 --> 00:01:59.367
-That was the advice.
-Wow!

00:01:59.367 --> 00:02:02.467
-There's one day
where Michelle --

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:04.667
In the scene in the movie,
it's cut down,

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:08.300
so you don't see so much of it,
but there's one day where

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:12.467
she's just sobbing
the whole day, like 14 hours.

00:02:12.467 --> 00:02:14.434
It's on action, she's sobbing.

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:17.400
On cut, she gets up and she's
like hydrating, I guess.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.801
[ Laughter ]
But she was doing that

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:24.434
the whole day and it's like
so powerful and so intense

00:02:24.434 --> 00:02:26.801
because it's real,
the whole day.

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:29.634
And the next day,
she's back to normal.

00:02:29.634 --> 00:02:33.000
And I remember I'm sitting
in like cast holding

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.334
and, you know,
she's like reading her script

00:02:37.334 --> 00:02:42.534
and I'm like in my chair,
like looking at her like,

00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:45.200
"How did you --
How did you do that?"

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.634
And she's like --
she has like a water bottle

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:47.701
and she's like...
[ Sniffs ]

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:51.267
"I don't know."

00:02:51.267 --> 00:02:52.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:53.934
-So, you're not getting
any advice

00:02:53.934 --> 00:02:55.300
from these great actors?
You're going,

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.901
[ Laughter ]
"Someone give me advice!

00:02:56.901 --> 00:02:58.467
I want to do what you're doing!"
-Yeah.

00:02:58.467 --> 00:03:00.300
-But then they probably
watch you and they go,

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:03.033
"Oh, I want advice from you,"
because you crushed it, buddy.

00:03:03.033 --> 00:03:05.000
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Well, thank you.
-You did a great job.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.334
-Thank you.
-You're fantastic.

00:03:06.334 --> 00:03:08.400
-Thank you so much.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.234
-Was there -- I mean,
there's so many tough scenes.

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:13.567
There's many funny scenes.

00:03:13.567 --> 00:03:15.367
You got punched in the nose.

00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:17.934
-Yeah.
-That was --
That was interesting.

00:03:17.934 --> 00:03:21.367
Seems that would be
your first action scenes.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.534
-I guess it's action,
action around me.

00:03:23.534 --> 00:03:24.767
-You're getting punched
in the --

00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:26.834
Yeah, getting punched is,
I mean, action, you --

00:03:26.834 --> 00:03:29.801
[ Laughter ]
-Yes, that's actually me
involved in the action.

00:03:29.801 --> 00:03:31.267
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:33.934
And Seth Rogen, I know, who's
also in the movie, he's great.

00:03:33.934 --> 00:03:35.300
-Oh, yeah.
-He was not in the scene,

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:36.868
but he was there, watching?

00:03:36.868 --> 00:03:38.200
-Yeah.
Like that was the fir--

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.234
So, there's a scene.
It's in the trailer,

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:42.167
so, I'm not spoiling anything.

00:03:42.167 --> 00:03:43.200
I get punched in the nose

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.767
and it's emotional,
it's intense.

00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:47.033
And, you know, there's a stunt
and there's extras

00:03:47.033 --> 00:03:49.467
and there's a mat
you have to fall down on
and there's blood.

00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:52.100
And it's very technical
and it's emotional.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:55.067
And, normally,
Steven does like four takes,

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:56.701
but we're doing like 12.

00:03:56.701 --> 00:03:59.834
And I'm thinking like,
"Something's not right,"

00:03:59.834 --> 00:04:02.934
and I'm trying to stay in it,
but it's like, okay.

00:04:02.934 --> 00:04:05.033
So, I'm like, "Is it me?
Is it me?"

00:04:05.033 --> 00:04:07.033
And so I get up and I'm like,
"Okay, I'm going to ask him,"

00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:09.367
and my head's down.
I'm trying to stay in it.

00:04:09.367 --> 00:04:10.767
Like, "What's going on?
What's going on?"

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:11.968
I round the corner

00:04:11.968 --> 00:04:14.767
and I see like Video Village
is all there.

00:04:14.767 --> 00:04:18.400
I look up and it's Seth Rogen,
like sitting in a yellow,

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.300
bright yellow T-shirt
in the monitor.

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:21.567
I'm like, "No, no, can't.

00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:23.033
[ Laughter ]
No, not right now."

00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:25.601
Like I can't meet him like this.
Like no way.

00:04:25.601 --> 00:04:27.467
-Yeah, because he's one
of your heroes?

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:28.667
-He's --

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:31.033
So, we're both from Vancouver.
-There you go.

00:04:31.033 --> 00:04:34.400
-Whoo!
-And Seth is a Vancouver icon.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:37.400
He was the voice of our SkyTrain
for a long time

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:40.367
[ Laughter and applause ]
and --

00:04:40.367 --> 00:04:44.734
[ Cheering ]

00:04:44.734 --> 00:04:46.667
And you'd be --
-Wow! Amazing, wow.

00:04:46.667 --> 00:04:48.133
[ Laughter and applause ]
You'd be sitting there --

00:04:48.133 --> 00:04:50.634
-To meet that, to meet the voice
of the SkyTrain.

00:04:50.634 --> 00:04:52.234
[ Laughter ]
Unbelievable.

00:04:52.234 --> 00:04:53.501
You'd be sitting there

00:04:53.501 --> 00:04:55.234
like on your phone
and it's like --

00:04:55.234 --> 00:04:56.701
Doon!
[ As Rogen ] Hi!

00:04:56.701 --> 00:04:59.300
[ Laughter ]
And you're like, "Okay."

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:01.133
-You did a pretty good "Hi,"
Seth Rogen, yeah.

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:02.901
I like that.
Not a high Seth Rogen,

00:05:02.901 --> 00:05:04.767
[ Laughter ]
but a hi from Seth Rogen, yeah.

00:05:04.767 --> 00:05:07.667
-It's a hi
from a high Seth Rogen.

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:09.501
-Yeah, it's a high
from a hi, yeah.

00:05:09.501 --> 00:05:11.534
-But, yeah,
and they named the octopus

00:05:11.534 --> 00:05:13.067
at the aquarium after him.

00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:15.033
[ Cheering ]
They named it Ceph Rogen,

00:05:15.033 --> 00:05:16.367
as in cephalopod.

00:05:16.367 --> 00:05:18.901
[ Laughter ]
And --
-Wow.

00:05:18.901 --> 00:05:21.400
Can't they just give him
a star or something?

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:22.501
Just give him anything, yeah.

00:05:22.501 --> 00:05:23.901
-And so -- But yeah, I mean,

00:05:23.901 --> 00:05:27.534
the impact he has
on Vancouver teenagers

00:05:27.534 --> 00:05:29.100
and me and my friends,
it's like religious.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:32.200
And so, when I got cast
and I was telling my friends

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:33.667
about it for the first time,
I was like,

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:35.000
"It's a Steven Spielberg movie."

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:37.501
They're like, "Uh-huh."
And I'm like, "And Paul Dano

00:05:37.501 --> 00:05:38.567
and Michelle Williams are
in it."

00:05:38.567 --> 00:05:39.400
They're like, "Uh-huh."

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:40.300
I'm like, "And Seth Rogen."

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:41.434
They go, "Seth Rogen?!"

00:05:41.434 --> 00:05:42.868
[ Cheering ]
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:42.868 --> 00:05:45.167
You're like, "Bigger than
Steven Spielberg, Seth Rogen?"

00:05:45.167 --> 00:05:47.267
Like, "He's the voice
of our tram system!"

00:05:47.267 --> 00:05:48.634
[ Laughter and cheering ]

00:05:48.634 --> 00:05:52.601
-Yeah, but, actually,
when I finished shooting

00:05:52.601 --> 00:05:54.267
and I saw my friends
for the first time,

00:05:54.267 --> 00:05:55.868
like over Christmas break,

00:05:55.868 --> 00:05:58.634
they like came up to me
and they're like,

00:05:58.634 --> 00:06:00.400
"Did you like smoke with him?"

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:01.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.901 --> 00:06:04.267
And like, "No, I'm working."

00:06:04.267 --> 00:06:05.934
And they're like, "Ahh!"

00:06:05.934 --> 00:06:07.334
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, "You missed it!"
-They're like, "Ahh!" Yeah.

00:06:07.334 --> 00:06:08.601
-"You missed it!"
Yeah.

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:11.701
Is there anything --
How do we set up the movie,

00:06:11.701 --> 00:06:14.000
for anyone, "The Fabelmans"?

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.968
-"The Fabelmans" is a story

00:06:16.968 --> 00:06:19.667
about Steven Spielberg's
upbringing

00:06:19.667 --> 00:06:21.334
and pretty much everything
that happens

00:06:21.334 --> 00:06:24.734
to my character, Sammy,
happened to Steven

00:06:24.734 --> 00:06:28.567
and it's about his family,

00:06:28.567 --> 00:06:30.534
about how he fell in love
with cinema.

00:06:30.534 --> 00:06:31.934
-Yeah.

00:06:31.934 --> 00:06:34.934
-I've seen this movie like
four times in packed audiences

00:06:34.934 --> 00:06:38.000
and it has --
it has an effect on people.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.234
And that's --
I'll just say that.

00:06:39.234 --> 00:06:40.467
-Yeah.
-It's really special.

00:06:40.467 --> 00:06:41.634
I want to show a clip.

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:43.868
Here's Gabriel LaBelle
in "The Fabelmans."

00:06:43.868 --> 00:06:45.167
Take a look.

00:06:45.167 --> 00:06:47.567
-$100 for a hobby?

00:06:47.567 --> 00:06:48.968
-It's not a hobby, Dad.

00:06:48.968 --> 00:06:51.367
-If you spent half the time
on algebra that you spend

00:06:51.367 --> 00:06:53.133
on these movies,
you could get --
-I hate algebra. Why are you --

00:06:54.667 --> 00:06:56.300
[ Scoffs ]
It's completely pointless.

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:57.601
-Not if you want
to make something,

00:06:57.601 --> 00:06:58.667
it's not pointless.

00:06:58.667 --> 00:07:00.634
Gee, Sammy, when I was a boy,

00:07:00.634 --> 00:07:02.267
I always used to think,
"Somebody figured out how

00:07:02.267 --> 00:07:03.534
to make this."
-Yeah.

00:07:03.534 --> 00:07:06.234
-This car, that rearview mirror,

00:07:06.234 --> 00:07:07.868
that directional signal.

00:07:07.868 --> 00:07:09.434
-I want to make movies, though!

00:07:09.434 --> 00:07:11.567
-That's right!
I want to make movies!

00:07:11.567 --> 00:07:12.734
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:07:12.734 --> 00:07:14.968
Gabriel LaBelle, everybody!

00:07:14.968 --> 00:07:17.167
[ Cheering and applause ]
You're fantastic in this.

00:07:17.167 --> 00:07:19.100
"The Fabelmans" is
in theaters now.

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.267
We'll be right back

00:07:20.267 --> 00:07:22.000
with a performance
from Manuel Turizo.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.300
Stick around, everybody.

